strategy set v1
# The opening range breakout (T01, ADR 0082) in eight variants, for the backtest job (scripts/backtest-dev.sh --set orb.set).
# It is not the live set: the live day and the prepare job read month.set. Trade the direction of the first candle of the session
# (5 or 15 minutes) on the twenty names whose volume in it is largest against their own normal, entered at a break of its high or low,
# stopped at a tenth or a fifth of the 14-day ATR, flat at 15:58. Risk 1 percent of the strategy's budget a trade; a position holds at
# most 5 percent of it. Shorts only in names the asset list says are easy to borrow.
balance 100000
loss 300 600
# The shared bars the candle is read from, for at most this many names (about 40 KB each).
bars 2000
# The paper's setting: a five minute candle, a stop at 10 percent of the ATR.
strategy 1 orb-5-10 t01 universe=universe-orb.spec
# A wider stop.
strategy 2 orb-5-20 t01 universe=universe-orb.spec stop_atr_pct=20
# The fifteen minute candle, which the paper found much weaker.
strategy 3 orb-15-10 t01 universe=universe-orb.spec range_minutes=15
strategy 4 orb-15-20 t01 universe=universe-orb.spec range_minutes=15 stop_atr_pct=20
# The same four with the hourly bias (T02, ADR 0083): a long only when the last completed hourly close is over the EMA(100) of hourly closes, a short
# only when under it. There is no bias before 10:30, so a break before then is no trade: compare each with its unfiltered twin above.
strategy 5 orb-5-10-bias t01 universe=universe-orb.spec bias=1
strategy 6 orb-5-20-bias t01 universe=universe-orb.spec stop_atr_pct=20 bias=1
strategy 7 orb-15-10-bias t01 universe=universe-orb.spec range_minutes=15 bias=1
strategy 8 orb-15-20-bias t01 universe=universe-orb.spec range_minutes=15 stop_atr_pct=20 bias=1
